BT /F1 11 Tf 54 800 Td 14 TL
(User authorization path description - KinetiQ BLE Diag \(individual developer\)) Tj T*
(========================================================================) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(App name: KinetiQ BLE Diag) Tj T*
(Package name: com.kinetiq.blediag) Tj T*
(App ID: 119406053) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Authorization flow:) Tj T*
(1. The user opens KinetiQ BLE Diag. The main screen shows, among other) Tj T*
(   diagnostic actions, one button labelled 'wearEngine probe'.) Tj T*
(2. When the user taps that button, the app calls the Wear Engine) Tj T*
(   requestPermission API. The Huawei Health app then displays the) Tj T*
(   standard system authorization screen which lists the requested) Tj T*
(   permission 'Basic device information'.) Tj T*
(3. The user taps Allow \(or Deny\) on the Health authorization screen.) Tj T*
(   The result is returned to the app, which shows one line of text) Tj T*
(   locally \(device list, or a failure note\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(No background or silent authorization is used, and authorization is) Tj T*
(never re-requested automatically; it happens only when the user taps) Tj T*
(the button. The user can revoke the permission at any time from the) Tj T*
(Huawei Health app settings or by denying the dialog.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Screenshots: the app's main screen \(showing the 'wearEngine probe') Tj T*
(button\) is attached. The Health authorization dialog itself appears) Tj T*
(only after the service application is approved; its standard layout) Tj T*
(will be used unchanged \(per attachment disabled during review\).) Tj T*
ET
